Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.78,0:00:20.81,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,In the depths of the black forest,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.65,0:00:30.13,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,hiding away in a house made of poisonous \Nmushrooms, there once lived a young witch.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.22,0:00:37.60,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,Although young, she had lived many times \Nlonger than humans who appeared her age.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.82,0:00:47.10,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,She had been living there alone ever since \Nshe was about half her current height.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.26,0:00:56.87,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,Recently, she'd taken an \Ninterest in making medicine.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.34,0:01:01.62,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,Working in a flow with the steam to \Nperform such a methodical task
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.62,0:01:03.86,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,seemed to put her mind at ease.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.86,0:01:09.65,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,Her medicines were effective against many \Nailments, and selling them in the nearby town
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.33,0:01:13.09,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,brought her some very welcome income.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.89,0:01:17.17,Default,Minos,0,0,0,,Luna, are we heading to town?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.98,0:01:18.79,Default,Luna,0,0,0,,Mm-hmm.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:33.86,0:01:35.90,Default,Minos,0,0,0,,You can ride on me, Luna.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:36.87,0:01:37.91,Default,Luna,0,0,0,,Maybe on the way home.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:37.91,0:01:40.95,Default,Minos,0,0,0,,It's fine with me, though. \NThis isn't heavy at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.66,0:01:43.88,Default - Top,Merino,0,0,0,,Have a nice trip!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.15,0:01:47.41,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,Once every three months, she took \Nthe medicine she made into town.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:47.41,0:01:50.99,Default,Minos,0,0,0,,Are you gonna buy more books with \Nthe money from the medicine?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:51.39,0:01:52.42,Default,Luna,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:52.42,0:01:56.91,Default,Minos,0,0,0,,You know what I think? I'd \Nlove a nice, warm, red vest.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:56.91,0:01:59.02,Default,Luna,0,0,0,,But I just knit you one a little while ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:59.02,0:02:03.89,Default,Minos,0,0,0,,Yeah, that old thing? It's so stiff and \Nscratchy, wearing it makes me wanna cry.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:03.89,0:02:07.45,Default,Minos,0,0,0,,But people say vests made from velvet \Ngoat wool are fluffy and soft
Dialogue: 0,0:02:07.45,0:02:09.73,Default,Minos,0,0,0,,and they still keep you nice and warm.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:09.73,0:02:13.02,Default,Luna,0,0,0,,Well, that's one way to \Ncomplain about Merino's wool.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:13.66,0:02:16.82,Default,Minos,0,0,0,,Aww, that's not what I mean. \NIt's just personal preference.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:16.82,0:02:20.45,Default,Minos,0,0,0,,I think my skin is more suited \Nto velvet wool, that's all.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.86,0:02:24.28,Default,Minos,0,0,0,,So when we get to town,\Ncan we visit the vest shop?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:37.33,0:02:42.47,Default,Luna,0,0,0,,I'll alter Merino's vest for you \Nso it feels more like velvet wool.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:42.47,0:02:46.73,Default,Minos,0,0,0,,But Luna, have you ever even felt \Nyarn made from velvet goats?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.73,0:02:50.48,Default,Minos,0,0,0,,If you don't know what it feels \Nlike, I kinda doubt you can copy it.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:51.91,0:02:56.56,Default,Minos,0,0,0,,We really should visit the vest shop \Nso you can see what it feels like.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:56.56,0:02:59.69,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,Wherever the witch walked or touched,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:59.69,0:03:02.54,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,she would often leave poisonous\N mushrooms in her wake.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.00,0:03:08.41,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,Thus, she was known in \Ntown as the Champignon Witch.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:42.78,0:04:46.99,Default - Top,text,0,0,0,,EPISODE 1: LUNA, THE BLACK WITCH
Dialogue: 0,0:04:42.87,0:04:45.59,Default,Minos,0,0,0,,I wonder if he'll let you touch a vest.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.59,0:04:47.01,Default,Luna,0,0,0,,I really doubt it.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.01,0:04:50.01,Default,Minos,0,0,0,,Because mushrooms might grow on it?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.47,0:04:53.02,Default,Mother,0,0,0,,Stay away from that!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.02,0:04:56.10,Default,Mother,0,0,0,,Don't get close to the black \Nwitch's poisonous mushrooms!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:56.10,0:05:00.05,Default,Mother,0,0,0,,There are people whose skin rotted \Naway after just touching one!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:00.52,0:05:03.34,Default,Towny 1,0,0,0,,Someone even died after \Naccidentally eating one.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:03.34,0:05:07.35,Default,Towny 2,0,0,0,,Yuck! They're releasing a strange\N gas. I bet it's poisonous!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:07.35,0:05:09.16,Default,Towny 3,0,0,0,,No, those are just spores.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:10.01,0:05:10.70,Default,Minos,0,0,0,,Hmm?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.83,0:05:14.37,Default,Minos,0,0,0,,Oh! It's the vest shop!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:15.78,0:05:19.54,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,The witch never felt very comfortable in town.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.43,0:05:24.60,Default,Luna,0,0,0,,Don't worry. I'll fix the other \Nvest and make it nice and soft.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.66,0:05:35.42,Default,Boy 1,0,0,0,,I thought so! The black witch's breath \Nand skin stink like poison gas!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:35.42,0:05:38.02,Default,Boy 2,0,0,0,,Get too close and you'll die!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:38.56,0:05:42.57,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,It was crowded places that bothered\N her more than the town itself.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:42.57,0:05:46.17,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,Things had been like this for as \Nlong as she could remember,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:46.17,0:05:51.58,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,so it had never made her particularly sad.\N It was just the way her body was.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.08,0:05:56.58,Default - Top,text,0,0,0,,MEDICINE
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.61,0:06:00.08,Default,Gilles,0,0,0,,Hmm? Oh, look who's here.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:00.08,0:06:04.34,Default,Gilles,0,0,0,,I just ran out of your hair growth \Nformula, so this is perfect timing.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:04.34,0:06:09.34,Default,Gilles,0,0,0,,People say it works very well, you know. \NWould you bring me a bigger batch next time?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:09.34,0:06:12.35,Default,Gilles,0,0,0,,I also need more of your back pain medicine.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.35,0:06:19.34,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,The apothecary was friendlier to the witch\N than most of the townspeople,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:20.75,0:06:23.56,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,as he both depended on the \Nwitch's pharmaceutical skills,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:22.31,0:06:24.01,Default - Top,Gilles,0,0,0,,Good. Here you go.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:24.01,0:06:26.78,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,and because he had some \Nknowledge of black witches.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:27.83,0:06:32.45,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,But whenever the witch visited, \Nhe always wore his herb-infused mask.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:33.37,0:06:36.97,Default,Gilles,0,0,0,,Oh, would you take those mushrooms \Nthat sprouted with you?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.37,0:06:41.33,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,It was just the way things were.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:45.10,0:06:47.45,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,The witch loved the bookstore.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:48.43,0:06:50.47,Default,Bookseller,0,0,0,,Oh. Please come in.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:52.07,0:06:56.89,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,Its owner was a descendant of \Nboth the human and spirit worlds,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:56.89,0:07:00.26,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,so he was also somewhat \Nunderstanding towards the witch.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.37,0:07:06.47,Default,Bookseller,0,0,0,,The town was bustling today \Nso I figured you'd be in.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:07.63,0:07:11.89,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,The townspeople were very suspicious \Nof both strangers and outsiders,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:11.89,0:07:14.31,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,so he lived his life in human form.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:16.01,0:07:17.41,Default,Bookseller,0,0,0,,Hmm? What's that for?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.41,0:07:21.88,Default,Bookseller,0,0,0,,Oh, are you checking out my true \Nform again? Please don't.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:22.63,0:07:24.57,Default,Bookseller,0,0,0,,I couldn't deal with you falling for me.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:25.37,0:07:29.00,Default,Minos,0,0,0,,Spirit types kinda have an attitude, don't they?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:29.34,0:07:31.00,Default,Bookseller,0,0,0,,I am glad you came, though.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:32.66,0:07:35.68,Default,Bookseller,0,0,0,,It's been quite some \Ntime since your last visit,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:36.13,0:07:40.69,Default,Bookseller,0,0,0,,so the air in town's grown stagnant. \NEven just stepping outside felt depressing.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:42.36,0:07:46.19,Default,Bookseller,0,0,0,,But thanks to your visit, maybe I can\N finally start venturing out again.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.51,0:07:51.87,Default,Bookseller,0,0,0,,You did absorb the poisons in town today, \Ndidn't you? Thank you, as always.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:52.89,0:07:54.20,Default,Bookseller,0,0,0,,But you know,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.93,0:07:59.92,Default,Bookseller,0,0,0,,the way your body reacts to pollution by \Ngrowing mushrooms that filter out toxins
Dialogue: 0,0:07:59.92,0:08:01.22,Default,Bookseller,0,0,0,,never ceases to amaze me.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:02.50,0:08:06.92,Default,Bookseller,0,0,0,,I'm sure it's rough on you and the mushrooms \Nthat have to carry that poison, though.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:07.42,0:08:12.51,Default,Luna,0,0,0,,A-A bunch of mushrooms sprouted in the town \Nsquare at the crossroads and surprised me.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:12.75,0:08:15.07,Default,Bookseller,0,0,0,,Oh. I think I know why.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:15.73,0:08:18.95,Default,Bookseller,0,0,0,,Last week, there was a public execution there.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:20.95,0:08:25.74,Default,Bookseller,0,0,0,,The criminal's regret and the crowd's \Noutrage must have saturated the area.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:25.74,0:08:30.10,Default,Bookseller,0,0,0,,The poisons from all of that \Nwickedness probably reacted to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:32.01,0:08:34.92,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,The bookstore owner did not state this outright,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:35.43,0:08:39.49,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,but a public execution meant \Nit was likely part of a witch hunt.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.53,0:08:46.69,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,It was also likely an acquaintance of \Nthe witch, and likely someone innocent,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:46.69,0:08:48.54,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,who was executed in the square.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:48.97,0:08:53.20,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,While this was still a small country, it \Nwas able to develop to the extent it had
Dialogue: 0,0:08:53.20,0:08:55.38,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,thanks to the help of powerful magicians.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.53,0:09:02.48,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,To maintain control over that power\N across generations, the royal family
Dialogue: 0,0:09:02.48,0:09:04.76,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,chose powerful white witches as their queens.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:05.91,0:09:08.68,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,As a result, those who were loyal to the crown
Dialogue: 0,0:09:08.68,0:09:13.34,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,were known as white witches and \Nwhite wizards, and those disloyal
Dialogue: 0,0:09:13.34,0:09:17.65,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,became known as black witches and black \Nwizards. Thus began the "Black Witch Hunt."
Dialogue: 0,0:09:20.58,0:09:21.61,Default,Bookseller,0,0,0,,Oh, right.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:22.29,0:09:23.08,Default,Luna,0,0,0,,Hmm?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:23.51,0:09:25.56,Default,Bookseller,0,0,0,,I got some good books in yesterday.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:26.08,0:09:27.15,Default,Luna,0,0,0,,Oh!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:27.51,0:09:31.18,Default,Bookseller,0,0,0,,I picked out a few that I thought \Nyou might be interested in.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:32.06,0:09:34.66,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,The world was a difficult place for the witch,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:35.09,0:09:37.40,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,but because she could still sell medicine
Dialogue: 0,0:09:37.89,0:09:41.72,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,and buy her dearly beloved \Nbooks in this human world,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:42.69,0:09:46.05,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,she had not completely given up on it yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:47.02,0:09:49.45,Default,Bookseller,0,0,0,,Six Pigous should just about cover it.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:50.54,0:09:52.18,Default,Bookseller,0,0,0,,Oh, they grew mushrooms!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:53.61,0:09:57.11,Default,Bookseller,0,0,0,,Money is full of bad energy, after all.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.62,0:10:02.87,Default,Bookseller,0,0,0,,Oh. Miss Witch, I have a favor to ask.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:02.87,0:10:08.15,Default,Bookseller,0,0,0,,I picked up a very strange book. It \Nseems to be under a very powerful curse.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:08.87,0:10:13.13,Default,Bookseller,0,0,0,,Word is that many of the people \Nwho read it went insane and died.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:13.42,0:10:15.62,Default,Bookseller,0,0,0,,I can't even pick it up.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:26.13,0:10:27.14,Default,Bookseller,0,0,0,,Miss Witch, watch out!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:39.55,0:10:40.29,Default,Luna,0,0,0,,Gulp.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:41.39,0:10:42.68,Default,Luna,0,0,0,,It's over.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:44.42,0:10:46.53,Default,Luna,0,0,0,,The book should be fine now.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:46.53,0:10:48.27,Default,Bookseller,0,0,0,,Th-Thanks.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:49.75,0:10:54.09,Default,Luna,0,0,0,,It tastes like that curse \Nkilled around 150 people.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:54.77,0:10:57.38,Default,Bookseller,0,0,0,,I don't ever want to know \Nwhat that tastes like.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:58.59,0:11:00.78,Default,Bookseller,0,0,0,,You really are something, Miss Witch.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:01.19,0:11:02.35,Default,Bookseller,0,0,0,,I appreciate the help.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:03.95,0:11:05.55,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,He did appreciate her,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:06.61,0:11:11.65,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,but as soon as she walked in, he was burning \Nherbal incense and wearing his crystal
Dialogue: 0,0:11:11.65,0:11:13.56,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,as he always did.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:13.56,0:11:19.05,Default,Bookseller,0,0,0,,Oh. And as thanks, you can read \Nthis. If you like it, it's yours.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:20.60,0:11:21.43,Default,Luna,0,0,0,,Bye.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:21.43,0:11:23.16,Default,Bookseller,0,0,0,,Yeah. Come back soon.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:24.97,0:11:28.16,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,The witch already knew that \Nwhen she left the store,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:28.57,0:11:33.86,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,the bookseller would start vigorously wiping \Ndown everything she had touched with lye.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:35.64,0:11:38.82,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,Still, she was grateful that \Nhe would wait until she left,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:38.82,0:11:43.58,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,indeed, that he would even let her in\N to begin with, so she paid it no mind.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:44.14,0:11:45.22,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,All was well.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:51.97,0:11:53.90,Default,Woman,0,0,0,,Finally!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:55.56,0:11:56.90,Default,Minos,0,0,0,,Luna?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.90,0:12:00.55,Default,Woman 1,0,0,0,,I'd been waiting for him to get \Nthis medicine back in stock!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:00.55,0:12:03.88,Default,Woman 2,0,0,0,,Now my bedridden mother can finally get better.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:04.41,0:12:08.62,Default,Woman 3,0,0,0,,I wish I could thank the person \Nwho makes this medicine.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:09.09,0:12:13.09,Default,Woman 4,0,0,0,,And selling it at a price we common \Nfolk can afford? What a blessing.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:17.42,0:12:19.63,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,The town was unpleasant in many ways,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:20.21,0:12:25.98,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,but it still offered unique moments like \Nthis that made her visits worthwhile.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:26.65,0:12:30.86,Default,Woman 5,0,0,0,,Thank goodness! Surely our child \Nwill get better with this.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:30.86,0:12:33.03,Default,Woman 6,0,0,0,,I wonder who brought it to us.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:33.44,0:12:38.23,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,This was not something she'd see if she \Nstayed hiding, alone, in her forest home.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:38.59,0:12:43.77,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,It was her reward for having the courage \Nto venture into the outside world.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:46.20,0:12:52.61,Default,Minos,0,0,0,,Luna, if they knew you made it, those people \Nprobably wouldn't buy your medicine anymore.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:52.61,0:12:56.99,Default,Minos,0,0,0,,But if that made you happy, I'm happy, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:57.86,0:13:03.12,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,It was as if all of her stress from enduring \None day in the city simply evaporated.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:03.12,0:13:07.47,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,For the witch, these moments \Nwere more magical than magic itself.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:26.99,0:13:29.99,Default - Top,text,0,0,0,,MEDICINE
Dialogue: 0,0:13:27.47,0:13:32.68,Default,Gilles,0,0,0,,A medicine that grows back \Nlegs? I can't sell that here!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:32.68,0:13:38.15,Default,Gilles,0,0,0,,If I started selling a medicine that \Nunusual, especially if it actually worked,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:38.15,0:13:41.50,Default,Gilles,0,0,0,,I'd have the authorities breathing \Ndown my neck in no time.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:42.25,0:13:46.26,Default,Gilles,0,0,0,,You shouldn't be making weird\N medicine in the first place.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:46.26,0:13:50.27,Default,Gilles,0,0,0,,You must remember you're still a black witch.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:50.27,0:13:53.45,Default,Gilles,0,0,0,,Let's see. One, two, three...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:53.45,0:13:56.47,Default,Gilles,0,0,0,,Hmm? Hey, what did I just tell you?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:56.47,0:13:58.45,Default,Gilles,0,0,0,,Subtlety isn't your strong suit, is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:00.01,0:14:04.84,Default,Minos,0,0,0,,I know how much work you put \Ninto that. You should be proud.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:06.28,0:14:10.23,Default,Minos,0,0,0,,Are you looking for the \None-legged man from before?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:13.57,0:14:16.87,Default,Minos,0,0,0,,You could ask someone, but I doubt \Nthey'd tell you where he is.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:16.87,0:14:20.23,Default,Minos,0,0,0,,If we find him, do you think \Nhe'd even accept the medicine?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:20.23,0:14:22.52,Default,Minos,0,0,0,,He might just run away like that guy.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:22.52,0:14:23.83,Default,Luna,0,0,0,,Hmm.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:26.80,0:14:28.33,Default,Minos,0,0,0,,Hmm.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:29.70,0:14:34.65,Default,Minos,0,0,0,,Are you gonna look anyway? Why not \Nask the bookseller or the apothecary?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:35.31,0:14:38.31,Default,Minos,0,0,0,,I could go for a cotton candy soda right now!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:37.23,0:14:39.74,Default - Top,Girl,0,0,0,,So, did you miss me?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:39.74,0:14:41.01,Default - Top,Henri,0,0,0,,You better believe I did.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:41.57,0:14:42.68,Default - Top,Girl,0,0,0,,I missed you, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:42.27,0:14:47.18,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,The first time the witch saw people \Nembracing and smiling like that,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:43.67,0:14:45.11,Default - Top,Henri,0,0,0,,Glad to hear it.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:47.41,0:14:49.59,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,she did not know what to make of it.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:50.82,0:14:56.83,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,Because when anyone touched her\N poisonous body, they soon regretted it.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:58.41,0:15:03.39,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,When someone touched her, their skin started \Nrotting and they stopped breathing,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:03.78,0:15:06.74,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,so people started avoiding her completely.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:10.59,0:15:14.85,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,The witch had never known\N the warmth of another's embrace.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:15.75,0:15:19.85,Default,Girl,0,0,0,,Hey, isn't that black witch \Nover there staring at us?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:20.13,0:15:24.25,Default,Henri,0,0,0,,Of course she is. Nobody can resist your beauty.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:24.25,0:15:26.28,Default,Girl,0,0,0,,Oh, stop it, Henri!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:27.59,0:15:32.64,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,She knew that this was known as "romance," \Nhaving learned it from her books.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:32.64,0:15:34.75,Default - Top,Girl,0,0,0,,But do you really mean it?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:34.75,0:15:36.37,Default - Top,Henri,0,0,0,,I'm the only one...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:35.35,0:15:39.42,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,A witch can do many things \Nthat humans cannot,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:39.42,0:15:43.34,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,but there are many common things that \Nhumans can do and witches cannot.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:45.13,0:15:47.86,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,Perhaps romance is one of those things.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:48.17,0:15:52.52,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,Still, the pros and cons all balanced out \Nin the end, so she paid it no mind.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:53.09,0:15:54.17,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,All was well.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:55.58,0:15:58.36,Default,Bookseller,0,0,0,,A middle-aged man with one leg missing?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:58.36,0:16:01.71,Default,Bookseller,0,0,0,,A lot of men ended up like \Nthat after the last war.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:02.10,0:16:03.40,Default,Bookseller,0,0,0,,I'll try asking around.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:05.62,0:16:08.36,Default,Bookseller,0,0,0,,By the way, what's going on with her?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:10.69,0:16:15.02,Default,Minos,0,0,0,,Well, we saw a boy and girl together \Nwhile searching and then that happened.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:15.02,0:16:16.87,Default,Bookseller,0,0,0,,That sounds like bull to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:16.87,0:16:18.33,Default,Minos,0,0,0,,Oh, {\i1}moo{\i0}!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:19.40,0:16:23.56,Default,Bookseller,0,0,0,,Oh. If you're looking for popular \Nromance novels, they're on that shelf.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:27.15,0:16:30.28,Default,Merino,0,0,0,,Luna! Minos!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:32.58,0:16:34.14,Default,Sisi,0,0,0,,Welcome home.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:34.46,0:16:36.18,Default,Merino,0,0,0,,Did you get any souvenirs?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:37.57,0:16:39.22,Default,Merino,0,0,0,,Show us the souvenirs you got!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:39.22,0:16:40.81,Default,Luna,0,0,0,,Once we get inside.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:40.81,0:16:43.22,Default,Sisi,0,0,0,,I betcha it's just more books.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:43.58,0:16:44.63,Default,Minos,0,0,0,,Bingo.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.63,0:16:46.04,Default,Merino,0,0,0,,Aww, again?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:46.04,0:16:50.43,Default,Minos,0,0,0,,Well, it's not her fault. Most shops \Nwon't even serve a black witch.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:50.43,0:16:54.32,Default,Merino,0,0,0,,Oh. I like the books with \Npictures and stuff, though.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:54.32,0:16:56.49,Default,Merino,0,0,0,,You got foam on your cheek.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:56.49,0:16:58.52,Default,Minos,0,0,0,,Yeah, that happens a lot in town.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:58.52,0:16:59.33,Default,Merino,0,0,0,,Does it really?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:00.11,0:17:04.65,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,Reading gave her a way to escape \Nthe world she was stuck in.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:05.35,0:17:08.76,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,She could enter the world of a \Nbook and become a someone else.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:10.38,0:17:15.57,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,The witch loved these moments, when \Nshe could escape from her troubles.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:16.10,0:17:19.70,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,In the books, humans who looked just like her
Dialogue: 0,0:17:20.33,0:17:23.22,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,but had no magic, went on \Ndangerous adventures...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:24.53,0:17:25.53,Default,Faces,0,0,0,,Oh.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:28.61,0:17:33.61,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,or gave research presentations, \Nliving through happiness and sadness.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:33.91,0:17:34.89,Default,Sisi,0,0,0,,Hmm.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:34.89,0:17:35.56,Default,Minos,0,0,0,,Oh.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:35.56,0:17:36.11,Default,Merino,0,0,0,,Ah!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:36.33,0:17:39.12,Default,Merino,0,0,0,,You were reading way over there?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:39.98,0:17:44.26,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,The witch used books to learn about \Nmany different life experiences.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:44.87,0:17:50.13,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,Though she could not do the same things \Nhumans could, she was not at all lonely.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:00.03,0:18:01.06,Default,Minos,0,0,0,,Luna,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:01.95,0:18:04.82,Default,Minos,0,0,0,,weren't you going to read a romance?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:06.75,0:18:10.46,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,Of course, love was one of \Nthose things out of her reach.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:14.65,0:18:18.17,Default,Minos,0,0,0,,Hey, hey, Luna. What's that story about?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:28.46,0:18:30.13,Default,Minos,0,0,0,,Whoa!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:31.49,0:18:33.34,Default,Sisi,0,0,0,,It's so pretty.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:44.81,0:18:47.18,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,The witch also liked to draw pictures.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:48.57,0:18:51.69,Default,Merino,0,0,0,,Luna, what are you drawing?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:52.79,0:18:54.69,Default,Minos,0,0,0,,Oh, I got it!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:55.02,0:18:58.19,Default,Minos,0,0,0,,It's the boy we saw with \Nthat girl in town today!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:58.67,0:19:00.33,Default,Merino,0,0,0,,That's so good!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:00.33,0:19:02.18,Default,Minos,0,0,0,,Looks just like him!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:02.18,0:19:06.29,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,To the witch, the boy she'd seen in town
Dialogue: 0,0:19:06.65,0:19:10.60,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,was even more beautiful than \Nthe princes in her books' illustrations.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:11.67,0:19:14.03,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,The witch loved beautiful things,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:14.49,0:19:18.72,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,but was always scared that her \Npoison would destroy that beauty.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:18.72,0:19:23.61,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,So if she liked something, she would sear \Nthe image in her mind, draw it later,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:23.61,0:19:26.86,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,and save the drawings. It was \None of her life's little pleasures.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:28.95,0:19:31.77,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,The witch put so much effort into \Nfaithful reproductions,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:29.48,0:19:31.48,Default - Top,Minos,0,0,0,,He's so handsome.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:32.19,0:19:34.73,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,her skill improved by leaps and bounds.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:36.23,0:19:39.79,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,Recently, when she put effort in,\N even if she hadn't intended it,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:40.27,0:19:42.66,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,her picture would sometimes take on a soul.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:42.66,0:19:45.48,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,This one was only a picture, \Nbut it was also more.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:47.24,0:19:53.39,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,It was the first time anyone \Nhad smiled to her so kindly.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:59.47,0:20:01.18,Default,Minos,0,0,0,,He's asking you to dance!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:01.18,0:20:02.76,Default,Merino,0,0,0,,Luna!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:10.45,0:20:11.40,Default,Merino,0,0,0,,Ah!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:13.45,0:20:14.77,Default,Merino,0,0,0,,Come on!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:19.23,0:20:23.14,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,The hand that emerged from the drawing \Nwas as cold and light as paper,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:23.59,0:20:28.52,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,but it was still the first time \Nthe witch had held someone's hand.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:33.04,0:20:35.54,Default - Top,Minos,0,0,0,,Have a good time!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:33.35,0:20:38.18,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,Her heart felt so light, it was \Nlike she could fly to the moon.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:38.77,0:20:44.05,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,The dance exceeded her wildest imagination. \NSomething that could only exist in books.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:44.05,0:20:45.55,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,It was a dream of a dance.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:47.29,0:20:49.56,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,Their serendipitous stroll in the night sky
Dialogue: 0,0:20:49.84,0:20:53.37,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,contained more romance than all \Nthe love stories in the world.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:53.87,0:20:57.55,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,It was more than a story. It was a miracle.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:08.69,0:21:09.93,Default,Merino,0,0,0,,Luna!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:25.37,0:21:27.38,Default,Merino,0,0,0,,Luna, are you okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:29.83,0:21:31.60,Default,Merino,0,0,0,,He turned back into paper.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:37.58,0:21:39.42,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,Like the moonlight itself,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:40.83,0:21:45.38,Italics,Lize,0,0,0,,that special night shone brightly in the \Nwitch's memory for the rest of her days.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:53.53,0:21:56.87,Default,Minos,0,0,0,,Are we going to buy more \Npencils and paper today?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:57.66,0:22:01.46,Default,Minos,0,0,0,,I know you drew a bunch\N of pictures of that boy.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:01.46,0:22:09.85,Default,Minos,0,0,0,,But only the first one came to life. Maybe \Nyou're starting to forget what he looks like.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:11.69,0:22:16.79,Default,Minos,0,0,0,,If you take a good look and draw him real \Nnice, maybe he'll come to life again.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:18.51,0:22:21.99,Default,Minos,0,0,0,,I hope they'll sell you the pencils and paper.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:24.34,0:22:29.42,Default,Minos,0,0,0,,Hey, Luna. If they let you buy \Na lot, you should draw me, too!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:29.42,0:22:35.12,Default,Minos,0,0,0,,Just make me look good. Like with \Nhorns three times this big.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:29.96,0:22:34.09,Default - Top,Girl,0,0,0,,So everything was just an act?\N I'm through with you!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:35.37,0:22:38.12,Default,Minos,0,0,0,,Oh. It's the couple from before.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:38.12,0:22:38.52,Default,Girl,0,0,0,,Hmph!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:38.52,0:22:43.82,Default,Minos,0,0,0,,But they seem kinda different. \NEspecially the boy.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:43.82,0:22:47.88,Default,Minos,0,0,0,,It's like the charm was sucked \Nout of him. He's an empty shell.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:47.88,0:22:49.98,Default,Girl,0,0,0,,You're never gonna believe it!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:50.62,0:22:53.85,Default,Girl,0,0,0,,Henri turned out to be a total loser!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:53.85,0:22:55.14,Default,Other girls,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:55.14,0:23:00.13,Default,Girl,0,0,0,,I don't need a guy like that. \NWhat in the world happened to him?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:01.38,0:23:05.90,Default,Girl,0,0,0,,Come to think of it, it started the day\N we saw that creepy black witch.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:06.29,0:23:07.49,Default,Minos,0,0,0,,Luna?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:11.73,0:23:13.54,Italics,Henri,0,0,0,,Sparkle, sparkle, sparkle, sparkle.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:16.81,0:23:17.55,Default,Henri,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:16.91,0:23:18.29,Default - Top,Girl,0,0,0,,Oh, come here!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:16.91,0:23:18.29,Overlap,Girl,0,0,0,,No, look at me!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:18.29,0:23:20.00,Default,Girl,0,0,0,,You're so cool!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:20.00,0:23:22.15,Default,Girl,0,0,0,,Let me see!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:22.15,0:23:24.18,Default,Girl,0,0,0,,You're so cute!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:24.18,0:23:24.60,Default,Henri,0,0,0,,Oh.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:24.60,0:23:26.42,Default,Girl,0,0,0,,I think I'm in love!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:26.06,0:23:27.42,Default - Top,Girl,0,0,0,,You're so cool!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:26.42,0:23:27.42,Default,Henri,0,0,0,,Ah!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:27.42,0:23:28.92,Default,Henri,0,0,0,,Hey, you there!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:29.66,0:23:30.47,Default,Henri,0,0,0,,Hold on!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:31.93,0:23:36.93,Default,Minos,0,0,0,,Luna, he's talking to you. And aren't \Nyou going to get pencils and paper?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:37.31,0:23:38.56,Default,Luna,0,0,0,,No, I'm not.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:38.56,0:23:41.74,Default,Luna,0,0,0,,I'm never drawing again.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:42.44,0:23:47.08,Default,Girl,0,0,0,,Come on, Henri. What's gotten into you, \Ngoing for a black witch like her?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:48.44,0:23:54.04,Default,Henri,0,0,0,,Uh... I'm not sure. It's like I totally\N forgot she was a black witch.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:54.82,0:23:58.15,Default,Henri,0,0,0,,She just seemed like a nice, \Nnormal, pretty girl to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:59.45,0:24:01.90,Default,Girl,0,0,0,,Eww, why would you say that?
Dialogue: 0,0:24:01.90,0:24:05.43,Default,Henri,0,0,0,,I don't know. I've never \Neven talked to her before.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:05.96,0:24:10.44,Default,Henri,0,0,0,,Next time I see her, maybe \NI should try talking to her again.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:12.01,0:24:15.14,Default - Top,text,0,0,0,,TRANSLATION: MICHAEL ARNOLD
Dialogue: 0,0:24:15.26,0:24:18.35,Default - Top,text,0,0,0,,SUBTITLE TIMING: ANDY ELLIS\NEDITING: ELISABETH CRIST
Dialogue: 0,0:24:18.72,0:24:23.10,Default - Top,text,0,0,0,,QUALITY CHECK: GABRIELLA ALABANZA\NTRANSLATION CHECK: MICHELLE TYMON
Dialogue: 0,0:25:43.62,0:25:47.25,Default - Top,text,0,0,0,,NEXT TIME: THE DESTINED ONE
